Model Response:
```json
{"thought":"I found that 'Super Strength' has power_id = 18. Now I need to write a Python script to join the superhero CSV with the hero_power table from the database, filter for heroes with Super Strength (power_id=18), and count those with height_cm > 200.","action":"execute_python","action_input":{"code":"import csv\nimport sqlite3\n\n# Read superhero data\nsuperheroes = {}\nwith open('csv/superhero.csv', 'r') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        hero_id = int(row['id'])\n        height = row['height_cm']\n        if height:  # Skip empty heights\n            try:\n                superheroes[hero_id] = int(height)\n            except ValueError:\n                pass\n\n# Connect to database and find heroes with Super Strength (power_id=18)\nconn = sqlite3.connect('db/hero_power.db')\ncursor = conn.cursor()\n\n# Get all hero_ids that have power_id=18 (Super Strength)\ncursor.execute(\"SELECT DISTINCT hero_id FROM hero_power WHERE power_id = 18\")\nsuper_strength_heroes = [row[0] for row in cursor.fetchall()]\nconn.close()\n\n# Count how many of these heroes have height > 200cm\ncount = 0\nfor hero_id in super_strength_heroes:\n    if hero_id in superheroes and superheroes[hero_id] > 200:\n        count += 1\n\nprint(f\"Heroes with Super Strength: {len(super_strength_heroes)}\")\nprint(f\"Heroes with Super Strength and height > 200cm: {count}\")"}}
```
